It draws the list, but my expectation was that it would check this variable for each one and choose the correct image accordingly.  What it does is, if an achievement is unlocked and I highlight the unlocked one, it changes all of them to the colored ones, then if I highlight a locked one, it changes them all to the locked image.  Game Variable 201 is an array, so I'm expecting it to check variable 201[1] for example, and if that is set to 1, draw the colored one, and check each individually.  It just checks for the first one and stops there.  I haven't actually found the DrawAllItems function yet though, I just assumed it was handled like a for loop.  I haven't gone back to it yet, but perhaps I should just use a for loop instead.
